// The Hunting expert - Hunter's skill master, at the north edge of the Feldip hunting grounds. He
// sells the Hunter cape to a player with 99 (skillcapes/scripts/skillcape_shop.rs2), and otherwise
// says what can be hunted here and with what: the two things a new hunter arriving at Feldip needs.
[opnpc1,hunting_expert]
if (~skillcape_offer(hunter) = true) {
    return;
}
~chatnpc("<p,happy>Welcome to the Feldip hunting grounds. Mind where you put your feet - there's more than one trap out here.");
@hunting_expert_menu;

[label,hunting_expert_menu]
switch_int (~p_choice3("What can I hunt here?", 1, "Where do I get traps?", 2, "Thanks, I'll be off.", 3)) {
    case 1 :
        ~chatplayer("<p,quiz>What can I hunt here?");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Birds, to start with. Lay a bird snare where the crimson swifts fly and one'll blunder into it sooner or later - any hunter can manage that. The tropical wagtails east of here want a bit more skill.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Down in the south-west corner there are Feldip weasels. Look in a burrow for tracks and follow them plant to plant - they always end in a bush. Then it's you, a noose wand and a quick hand.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>The boulders through the middle of the grounds make good deadfalls, if you've a knife and some logs. Wild kebbits nose around the southern ones; the barb-tailed ones up north are warier, but that tail makes a fine harpoon.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>And the pits - lay spiked logs over one, poke a larupia with a teasing stick, and jump the pit with it after you. If it's close behind when you land, in it goes. If not, well. Mind your ankles.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>There are pits on Karamja too, west of Shilo Village, where the horned graahks graze. Same trick, bigger horns. There's usually a teasing stick lying about down there.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Once you're handier, try a box trap. Ferrets in the north-west, chinchompas in the clearing to the south, and the carnivorous ones north-east of those - but keep your fingers away from those.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Further afield there's net trapping: a small fishing net and a rope on a young tree, and whatever runs across the net ends up hanging from it. Swamp lizards in the swamp south-east of Canifis, orange salamanders among the rocks north-west of Uzer.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Red salamanders by the lake past the Khazard battlefield, and black ones in the Bone Yard - that's the Wilderness, mind. And don't stand on your own net; nothing will cross it while you're on it.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>That same patch of desert north-west of Uzer has golden warblers for your snares - noisy things - and desert devils. Look in a burrow there and follow the tracks from cactus to rockslide; they always end in a patch of disturbed sand.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>And north-east of Rellekka, past the Keldagrim entrance, there's snow country: polar kebbits, blue-feathered twitches, sabre-toothed kebbits for a deadfall and kyatts for a pit. There's a fellow up on the plateau who knows it better than I do.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>The best of it is imps. Lay a magic box where they wander - anywhere, they're everywhere - and one'll blunder in. It takes a practised hand, mind, and don't stand on the box.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>A caught imp will take things to your bank for you, twice, if you ask it nicely. Beads make good bait - they love the things.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Stay near your traps. Wander off and they'll collapse, and nothing walks into a trap it knows you couldn't hold it with.");
        @hunting_expert_menu;
    case 2 :
        ~chatplayer("<p,quiz>Where do I get traps?");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Aleck's Hunter Emporium in Yanille, north of here, has everything: nets, jars, snares, box traps, magic boxes. Leon in the back sells a crossbow, if you're that way inclined.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Nearer to hand, the ogre trader in Gu'Tanoth keeps box traps, bird snares, teasing sticks and noose wands, strange as that sounds. Ogres do love a trap.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Nets and rope for a net trap you'll find nearer the lizards: the general stores in Canifis, Port Khazard and Edgeville, and the shop at the Shantay Pass.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>And if you're out in the desert, Artimeus in Nardah keeps a proper Hunter shop: snares, box traps, noose wands, the lot.");
        @hunting_expert_menu;
    case 3 :
        ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Thanks, I'll be off.");
        ~chatnpc("<p,happy>Good hunting.");
}
